        "original_id": "f31a66d8-2b4d-52f0-a892-9accd100d9af",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Tivolis Koncertsal, Tivoli Gardens, Copenhagen, Denmark, Klampenborg\n- Products: Tivoli Two\n- People: Duke Jordan\n- Organizations: SteepleChase\n- Topics: amusement parks, live albums\n\nFacts:\n- Tivoli Gardens opened on 15 August 1843.\n- Tivoli Gardens is the second-oldest operating amusement park in the world after Dyrehavsbakken in nearby Klampenborg, Denmark.\n- Tivolis Koncertsal is a 1,660-capacity concert hall located at Tivoli Gardens in Copenhagen, Denmark.\n- Tivoli Two is a live album by Duke Jordan's Trio that was recorded at Tivolis Koncertsal.\n- Tivoli Two was first released in 1984 on the Danish SteepleChase label.",
